-- Sūrat al-Aḥqāf (46) cut into study passages (drill-engine plan Phase 3.3): until now it had none,
-- so it could not be opened. Every boundary is the mufassirūn's: al-Rāzī's multi-āyah units are the
-- spine (10 of his 11 blocks group āyāt), checked against Ibn ʿĀshūr, al-Zamakhsharī and al-Ālūsī,
-- with al-Ṭabarī, Ibn Kathīr, Ibn ʿAṭiyya and Abū Ḥayyān as corroboration; and the iʿrāb books
-- (al-Jadwal, al-Iʿrāb al-Muyassar) on whether each boundary's opening sentence is resumptive
-- (istiʾnāf) or joined (ʿaṭf). A resumptive sentence alone does not cut — they occur mid-passage
-- (5, 12) — it decides where the tafsīr also turns. Where the works disagree the wider grouping is
-- kept and the dissent written in meta_json.boundary_evidence. Strongest: 29-32 (four works), 15-16
-- and 13-14 (three). Covers 1-35 with no gap and no overlap.

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO qr_surah_study_passage
  (id, surah, passage_no, ayah_from, ayah_to, public_unit_id, public_surah_unit_id, label, title_en, title_ar,
   subtitle, theme, summary_md, start_ref, end_ref, meta_json, status)
VALUES
('QR:SP:46:1-3', 46, 1, 1, 3, 'U:C:QURAN:46:1-3', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 1', 'The Book Sent Down, and Creation in Truth', 'تَنْزِيلُ الكِتَابِ وَخَلْقٌ بِالحَقِّ', '46:1–3', 'tanzil_and_creation_in_truth', 'The sūra opens on the Book sent down from God, the Mighty, the Wise, and on a creation made with truth and a fixed term. Those who deny turn away from what they are warned of.', '46:1', '46:3', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 1, "boundary_evidence": "zamakhshari 1-3; ibn_ashur says at 4 «انتقل إلى الاستدلال على بطلان صفة الإلهية عن أصنامهم» (a new movement); the iʿrāb books give 4 (قل أرأيتم) no link to what precedes. Dissent: razi 1-4 and tabari 1-4; ibn_ashur and alusi 1-2", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:4-6', 46, 2, 4, 6, 'U:C:QURAN:46:4-6', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 2', '“Show Me What They Created”', 'أَرُونِي مَاذَا خَلَقُوا', '46:4–6', 'challenge_to_the_idols', 'The proof that the idols are no gods: they created nothing on earth, hold no share in the heavens, and no book or trace of knowledge backs them. Between the proof''s parts, a wonder at those who call on what cannot answer and will disown them on the Day.', '46:4', '46:6', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 2, "boundary_evidence": "ibn_ashur: 4 opens the proof against the idols, 5-6 an interjection (اعتراض) inside it; ibn_kathir 1-6 and ibn_atiyya 1-6 close at 6. Dissent: razi 5-8, zamakhshari 6-7; jadwal and muyassar read 5 as resumptive", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:7-10', 46, 3, 7, 10, 'U:C:QURAN:46:7-10', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 3', '“Plain Magic”, “He Forged It” — and the Answer', 'هَذَا سِحْرٌ مُبِينٌ… أَمْ يَقُولُونَ افْتَرَاهُ', '46:7–10', 'charge_of_forgery_answered', 'Read the verses, they call them plain magic and say the Prophet forged them. He answers that he is no novelty among the messengers and follows only what is revealed to him, and a witness from the Children of Israel has already borne witness.', '46:7', '46:10', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 3, "boundary_evidence": "ibn_kathir 7-9 and ibn_atiyya 7-9 open at 7; jadwal reads 7 as resumptive; ibn_ashur reads 9 as the reply to «افتراه» (8), 10 continuing it (فاء عاطفة in jadwal); razi groups 9 with 10. Dissent: muyassar reads 7 as joined (عاطفة); razi 5-8 and 9-12; ibn_kathir and ibn_atiyya open a unit at 10", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:11-14', 46, 4, 11, 14, 'U:C:QURAN:46:11-14', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 4', '“Had It Been Good, They Would Not Have Beaten Us to It”', 'لَوْ كَانَ خَيْرًا مَا سَبَقُونَا إِلَيْهِ', '46:11–14', 'pride_against_the_believers', 'Another of their errors, born of pride: they judge Islam by who reached it first. The Book of Mūsā went before this Arabic Book that confirms it, and those who say “Our Lord is God” and then stand firm have nothing to fear.', '46:11', '46:14', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 4, "boundary_evidence": "zamakhshari 11-14 exactly; ibn_ashur: 11 «حكاية خطأ آخر من أخطاء حجج المشركين»; jadwal reads 11 as resumptive; razi, ibn_ashur and tabari all group 13-14 inside it. Dissent: razi 9-12, ibn_kathir 10-14; muyassar reads 11 as joined", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:15-16', 46, 5, 15, 16, 'U:C:QURAN:46:15-16', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 5', 'The Son Who Gives Thanks', 'وَوَصَّيْنَا الإِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ', '46:15–16', 'the_grateful_son', 'The charge to do good to parents: the mother who carried and bore him in hardship, and the son who at forty asks to be thankful for the favour on him and on them. Their best deeds are accepted and their misdeeds passed over.', '46:15', '46:16', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 5, "boundary_evidence": "razi 15-16 AND zamakhshari 15-16 AND ibn_kathir 15-16 (three works exactly); jadwal reads 15 as resumptive", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:17-20', 46, 6, 17, 20, 'U:C:QURAN:46:17-20', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 6', 'The Son Who Says “Uff”', 'وَالَّذِي قَالَ لِوَالِدَيْهِ أُفٍّ لَكُمَا', '46:17–20', 'the_defiant_son', 'The other son mocks his parents'' warning of the resurrection as tales of the ancients. To each there are ranks for what they did, and on the Day the deniers are set before the Fire they are told they spent their good things in the life of this world.', '46:17', '46:20', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 6, "boundary_evidence": "razi 17-20 AND ibn_kathir 17-20 exactly; zamakhshari 17-18 inside it; jadwal reads 17 as resumptive. Dissent: ibn_ashur marks 20 as «انتقال إلى وعيد الكافرين», jadwal and muyassar read 20 as resumptive, abu_hayyan 20-26, ibn_atiyya 20-22", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:21-26', 46, 7, 21, 26, 'U:C:QURAN:46:21-26', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 7', 'The Brother of ʿĀd at al-Aḥqāf', 'وَاذْكُرْ أَخَا عَادٍ إِذْ أَنْذَرَ قَوْمَهُ بِالأَحْقَافِ', '46:21–26', 'hud_and_ad', 'Hūd warns his people among the sand dunes; they ask for the punishment they are promised, take the coming cloud for rain, and it is the wind that destroys all. The lesson drawn: they had more power, hearing, sight and hearts than you, and none of it availed them.', '46:21', '46:26', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 7, "boundary_evidence": "razi 21-26 exactly, abu_hayyan 20-26; ibn_ashur: 21 «سيقت قصة هود… مساق الموعظة», 26 «استخلاص لموعظة»; jadwal and muyassar read 21 as resumptive. Dissent: ibn_kathir 21-25 (26 with 27-28)", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:27-28', 46, 8, 27, 28, 'U:C:QURAN:46:27-28', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 8', 'The Towns Destroyed Around You', 'وَلَقَدْ أَهْلَكْنَا مَا حَوْلَكُمْ مِنَ القُرَى', '46:27–28', 'ruined_towns_around_you', 'ʿĀd were not alone: the towns around Makka were destroyed too, and the signs set out in turn so they might return. The gods they took as a means of nearness did not help them; they vanished from them.', '46:27', '46:28', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 8, "boundary_evidence": "razi 27-28 AND tabari 27-28 exactly; ibn_ashur: 27 follows the parable of ʿĀd with others like it. Dissent: ibn_kathir 26-28, ibn_atiyya 27-29", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:29-32', 46, 9, 29, 32, 'U:C:QURAN:46:29-32', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 9', 'The Jinn Who Listened', 'وَإِذْ صَرَفْنَا إِلَيْكَ نَفَرًا مِنَ الجِنِّ', '46:29–32', 'the_jinn_listen', 'A band of jinn is turned toward the Prophet, hears the Qurʾān, falls silent, and goes back to warn its people: a Book sent down after Mūsā, confirming what came before and guiding to the truth. Answer God''s caller.', '46:29', '46:32', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 9, "boundary_evidence": "razi 29-32 AND ibn_ashur 29-32 AND zamakhshari 29-32 AND ibn_kathir 29-32 (four works exactly); jadwal and muyassar read 29 as resumptive", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live'),
('QR:SP:46:33-35', 46, 10, 33, 35, 'U:C:QURAN:46:33-35', 'U:C:QURAN:46', 'Passage 10', 'Able to Give the Dead Life — So Be Patient', 'بِقَادِرٍ عَلَى أَنْ يُحْيِيَ المَوْتَى… فَاصْبِرْ', '46:33–35', 'resurrection_and_patience', 'Back to the resurrection: the One not wearied by creating the heavens and the earth can give the dead life, and the deniers set before the Fire will confess it. Then the close: be patient as the messengers of resolve were; to the deniers their stay will seem an hour of a day.', '46:33', '46:35', '{"source": "tafsir-boundaries", "order_index": 10, "boundary_evidence": "ibn_kathir 33-35 exactly; razi 33-34 then 35; ibn_ashur: 33 «عود إلى الاستدلال على إمكان البعث», 35 «تفريع على ما سبق في هذه السورة». Dissent: razi and ibn_ashur treat 35 as the sūra''s close on its own; abu_hayyan 27-35", "irab_books": ["qul_jadwal_irab_quran", "qul_irab_muyassar"]}', 'live');
